{"data":{"id":"f3bkx","type":"nodes","attributes":{"title":"When Internal Signals Mislead: Sensing and Preference in Artificial Homeostasis","description":"Author: Jonathan D Faeth. Affiliation: Independent Researcher.\n\nThis simulation study tests whether coupled selective sensing and assumed likelihood precision differ from preference reweighting in robustness to misleading internal signals. In the AffectWorld platform, three agent configurations will be evaluated under clean, positively biased, and symmetric-perturbation conditions across 12 fixed layouts and 64 new seeds (6,912 episodes). The primary outcome is a 40-step resource-regulation loss including a terminal-failure penalty. The primary estimand is the seed-paired difference between coupled and preference agents in bias-minus-clean loss, with a two-sided 95% Student-t interval. Earlier exploratory simulations informed the design and are excluded from confirmation. This is an empirical extension of prior artificial-homeostasis research; subjective experience and consciousness are not measured.","category":"","custom_citation":null,"date_created":"2026-09-29T16:26:34.378934","date_modified":"2026-10-02T04:04:26.128468","registration":false,"preprint":false,"fork":false,"collection":false,"tags":["artificial homeostasis"],"access_requests_enabled":true,"node_license":{"copyright_holders":[],"year":""},"analytics_key":"","current_user_can_comment":false,"current_user_permissions":["read"],"current_user_is_contributor":false,"current_user_is_contributor_or_group_member":false,"wiki_enabled":true,"public":true,"subjects":[[{"id":"584240d954be81056ceca9a1","text":"Physical Sciences and Mathematics"}]]},"relationships":{"license":{"links":{"related":{"href":"https://api.osf.io/v2/licenses/563c1cf88c5e4a3877f9e96a/","meta":{}}},"data":{"id":"563c1cf88c5e4a3877f9e96a","type":"licenses"}},"children":{"links":{"related":{"href":"https://api.osf.io/v2/nodes/f3bkx/children/","meta":{}}}},"collected_in":{"links":{"rel